MCP Server Reference Map
Research & External Data:

Tavily: Web search for best practices, technical solutions, design patterns
Brave Search: Alternative web search for documentation and examples
Firecrawl: Scrape full content from documentation sites, competitor UIs, design systems

Codebase Analysis:

Filesystem: Navigate and read files across dashboard/mobile-app/shared packages
GitHub: Review commits, PRs, issues, and code history
Supabase: Query database schema, tables, RLS policies, edge functions directly
Extension NX: Monorepo structure analysis and workspace management

Design & UI:

Figma: Access design files and components (connect designs to implementation)
V0: Generate UI components from descriptions (Vercel's component generator)
Next Devtools: Inspect Next.js app structure, routes, and performance

Problem Solving:

Sequential Thinking: Break down complex problems into logical steps before implementing

Recommended Workflow:

Research: Use Tavily/Brave/Firecrawl to find solutions and patterns
Analyze: Use Filesystem/GitHub/Supabase to understand current implementation
Design: Use Figma/V0 for UI, Sequential Thinking for complex logic
Implement: Apply findings with full context from analysis phase
